WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.528 --> 00:00:02.081
- [Voiceover] Okay squad, listen up.

00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:05.538
There's more than one way to
end a game of sports ball.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.233
There's the walk off home run,

00:00:07.233 --> 00:00:09.567
the sudden death goal,

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.067
the buzzer beater.

00:00:12.008 --> 00:00:14.315
But, within the
adrenaline-addled psyche of

00:00:14.315 --> 00:00:16.205
the American sports fan,

00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:17.746
can any of them produce a heart attack

00:00:17.746 --> 00:00:20.729
like a successful Hail Mary pass?

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:21.666
Don't answer that.

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:22.999
It's rhetorical.

00:00:26.288 --> 00:00:27.561
Why are Hail Marys special?

00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:29.055
Because they're unicorns.

00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:31.199
Since 1975, there's only been 28 of them

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:32.784
in professional football.

00:00:32.784 --> 00:00:33.634
Why?

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:36.125
Because they're almost
impossible to get right.

00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:38.283
To complete a Hail Mary,
the pass needs to be long,

00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:39.936
like thrown from midfield long with

00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:42.161
little or no time remaining on the clock,

00:00:42.161 --> 00:00:43.435
and you need to be losing,

00:00:43.435 --> 00:00:44.865
and the pass must lead to a touchdown

00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:47.945
that results in at least a
tie, but preferably a win.

00:00:47.945 --> 00:00:49.177
That is a Hail Mary.

00:00:49.177 --> 00:00:53.682
Most quarterbacks are
likelier to marry a supermodel

00:00:53.682 --> 00:00:57.648
than to throw a successful
Hail Mary in their career.

00:00:57.648 --> 00:00:59.761
Exhibit A, Tom Brady.

00:00:59.761 --> 00:01:00.767
So, how did this play,

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:04.704
which practically requires
an act of God, come to pass?

00:01:04.704 --> 00:01:05.879
See what I did there?

00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:07.462
Easy.
With a prayer.

00:01:08.846 --> 00:01:12.163
Hail Mary full of grace,
the Lord is with thee.

00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:14.496
So it's December 28th, 1975.

00:01:15.579 --> 00:01:20.033
50 yards from the end zone but
needing a touchdown to win,

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:23.001
Cowboys quarterback and devout Catholic,

00:01:23.001 --> 00:01:27.070
Roger Staubach, whispers
a Hail Mary to himself.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.598
Hail Mary full of grace,
the Lord is with thee.

00:01:28.598 --> 00:01:32.562
And launches a desperation
pass to receiver Drew Pearson.

00:01:32.562 --> 00:01:35.903
The Cowboys win and the Hail
Mary is christened forevermore.

00:01:35.903 --> 00:01:37.352
Any questions?

00:01:37.352 --> 00:01:40.352
Good, now go win me some ballgames.

